{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03537",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.59,
      "end_seconds": 4.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Actually, hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.21,
      "end_seconds": 8.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.63,
      "end_seconds": 13.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "It's no symptoms, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.75,
      "end_seconds": 16.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.02,
      "end_seconds": 27.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.81,
      "end_seconds": 46.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.6, saturation 98 percent, BP is 112 over 78, pulse is 66 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.76,
      "end_seconds": 52.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.06,
      "end_seconds": 59.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination. Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.75,
      "end_seconds": 66.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "Ah, I'd say two months. Actually, no, closer to about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.89,
      "end_seconds": 72.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "So, would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.28,
      "end_seconds": 75.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Mostly severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.89,
      "end_seconds": 80.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Any a low blood count on a routine test as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.27,
      "end_seconds": 85.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Yeah. About three months, you know, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.27,
      "end_seconds": 91.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Any blood in the stool, black stools or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.69,
      "end_seconds": 101.26,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "No blood in the stool, black stools or weight loss, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.07,
      "end_seconds": 105.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Okay, what about heavy periods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.8,
      "end_seconds": 107.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Nope, no heavy periods."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.64,
      "end_seconds": 112.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.2,
      "end_seconds": 117.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "I mean, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.97,
      "end_seconds": 136.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.19,
      "end_seconds": 138.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.4,
      "end_seconds": 140.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.35,
      "end_seconds": 145.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.86,
      "end_seconds": 149.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.11,
      "end_seconds": 154.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.26,
      "end_seconds": 159.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.45,
      "end_seconds": 163.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.6,
      "end_seconds": 166.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.5,
      "end_seconds": 171.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.13,
      "end_seconds": 175.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.47,
      "end_seconds": 184.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.04,
      "text": "I mean, I had a mole taken off my arm a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.02,
      "end_seconds": 192.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.01,
      "end_seconds": 199.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "It's lamotrigine, 100 milligrams, maybe, twice a day for the fits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.64,
      "end_seconds": 204.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.31,
      "end_seconds": 210.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.67,
      "end_seconds": 225.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.94,
      "end_seconds": 232.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "I have epilepsy. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.02,
      "end_seconds": 236.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Okay, may I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.09,
      "end_seconds": 249.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.49,
      "end_seconds": 253.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.77,
      "end_seconds": 267.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Your pulse and blood pressure are normal, and the eyelids are pale."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.47,
      "end_seconds": 286.65,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "Please sit back down. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is iron-deficiency anaemia needing a source found. Another possibility is a bowel cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.82,
      "end_seconds": 292.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Oh, I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.63,
      "end_seconds": 319.25,
      "duration_seconds": 25.62,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's iron-deficiency anaemia needing a source found, and we'll know more once the a camera test of the stomach and bowel is back. Just to be sure I understood. You've had no symptoms for about a month, severe, and no weight loss or black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.15,
      "end_seconds": 323.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Erm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.33,
      "end_seconds": 358.19,
      "duration_seconds": 32.86,
      "text": "I'm going to order a camera test of the stomach and bowel, for iron-deficiency anaemia. We'll begin with ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day, three months. You take it by mouth. It's for iron deficiency. Stop the ibuprofen and we will refer you for scopes. I think the lower GI team should see you too. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.04,
      "end_seconds": 360.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Okay, makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.78,
      "end_seconds": 381.56,
      "duration_seconds": 18.78,
      "text": "An iron study is something we might do if this doesn't improve in a month. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. Come back after the tests. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.24,
      "end_seconds": 386.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}